":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I approve PKT-0028. I read the packet and the full test file; I did not rerun the acceptance commands, because the factory already ran them on this commit.\n\n**Goal coverage**\n- **Auth with missing data:** no name gives \"Anonymous\" (also with a first name only). Missing permissions gives an editor, and `edit: false` gives a viewer. A user with no `id` is stored with the id `\"undefined\"`. A message missing `user` or `token` is silently ignored. A database error during auth gives ACCESS_DENIED and a disconnect.\n- **Missing tenant:** this is only covered by the \"connection without handshake\" test. That test pins the TypeError, the drop reason and the disconnect. It is the weakest part of the goal, but it is acceptable.\n- **Client disconnect during auth or save:** both paths are pinned with promises that are held open, then the connection is closed. The tests check the right things: nothing is registered and nothing is inserted. The two last-editor cases are also pinned: a disconnect waits 5 s before saving (`utils.sleep` is spied and checked for `[[5000]]`), and an explicit `close` saves at once while the later disconnect does nothing.\n- **File streaming:** a client abort and an ECONNRESET both resolve, and a storage error rejects.\n- **Forcesave after close:** replies NotModified through the socket. The direct `startForceSave(Form)` call with a connection that has no user rejects with a TypeError. The Command path gives DocumentIdError, then NotModified.\n\n**Characterization quality**\n- The current behaviour is recorded as it is, not fixed: every wrong behaviour has its own test, tagged `crash-prone: P4 target`.\n- The assertions are concrete: exact codes, `disconnect(true)`, log patterns, call counts.\n- All 5 surprising behaviours in the Executor log are kept in tests.\n- No source file changed, so nothing in the contract changed.\n- Budget: 3 files and 588 lines, within the limits of 6 files and 800 lines.\n\n**Process (TEP-0004)**\n- The Executor log is filled in.\n- No follow-up packet was requested, with a reason given (P4 already exists in the plan and depends on this one).\n- The Lessons for the Atlas and the friction line are present.\n\n**Minor points, not blocking**\n- `wopiClient.js:1212` streams without the protection and is left uncharacterized. The executor declared this openly.\n- Prettier was not checked on the new file because the command was refused, but the lint check passes.\n- Some tests rely on module state shared across the suite; unique document ids limit how much one test can affect another.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE The goal's crash paths are pinned with concrete assertions, every wrong behaviour is tagged as a P4 target, no source changed and the budget is respected.","ttft_ms":2402,"type":"result","duration_ms":16565,"uuid":"04f6094d-63ed-43ad-927a-2851d9a2423b","ttft_stream_ms":1093,"time_to_request_ms":352,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":8,"system_prompt":173,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":23,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":32,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":9,"init_frame_send":4,"engine_pickup":2,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":3,"request_announcements":14,"query_setup":5,"auto_mode_context_wait":9,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":34,"message_normalization":4,"client_creation":7,"request_build":12},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":82,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":238,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":215,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":140,"process_rss_mib_result":227,"process_anon_mib_result":138,"process_peak_rss_mib":259,"process_cpu_ms_turn":1055,"process_wall_ms_turn":16564,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":375,"process_wall_ms_streaming":13576,"main_stream_count":4,"main_stream_event_count":258,"main_stream_chunk_count":88,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":